# Synphony Deployment Finance OS — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in DATABASE_URL before running anything —
# see README.md > Quick start.

# --- Database (required) ----------------------------------------------------
# A Postgres connection string. Any Postgres works: a free Neon/Supabase project,
# Railway Postgres, or a local server (e.g. `createdb synphony` on a machine
# running Postgres, then postgresql://<your-username>@localhost:5432/synphony).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/synphony"

# --- Auth (optional, future) -------------------------------------------------
# The MVP uses a first-party cookie session (see src/lib/auth/session.ts) with
# bcrypt-hashed demo passwords seeded by `npm run db:seed`. To swap in a
# production auth provider (Supabase Auth, Clerk, NextAuth), add its required
# variables here, e.g.:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""

# --- Server Actions (optional, production deploys behind a proxy/CDN) ------
# NEXT_SERVER_ACTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""
